1. Check Git Installation
Command	Purpose
git --version	Check Git version
git --help	Display Git help
git help <command>	Help for a specific command

Example

git --version

2. Git Configuration (One-Time Setup)
Command	Purpose
git config --global user.name "Your Name"	Set username
git config --global user.email "email@example.com"	Set email
git config --list	Display Git configuration

Example

git config --global user.name "Geetha Priya"
git config --global user.email "yourmail@gmail.com"

3. Create or Clone Repository
Command	Purpose
git init	Create a new Git repository
git clone <URL>	Copy a repository from GitHub

Example

git init

or

git clone https://github.com/geethapriyar30/Data_Engineering_GP.git

4. Check Repository Status
Command	Purpose
git status	Show changed files
git log	Show commit history
git log --oneline	Compact commit history

Example

git status


5. Add Files (Staging)
Command	Purpose
git add file.txt	Add one file
git add .	Add all files
git add *.py	Add all Python files

Example

git add .

6. Commit Changes
Command	Purpose
git commit -m "message"	Save a version
git commit -am "message"	Add modified tracked files and commit

Example

git commit -m "Added Git notes"


7. Connect to GitHub
Command	Purpose
git remote add origin URL	Connect local repo to GitHub
git remote -v	Show remote repository
git remote remove origin	Remove remote

Example

git remote add origin https://github.com/geethapriyar30/Data_Engineering_GP.git

8. Upload & Download
Command	Purpose
git push	Upload changes
git push origin main	Push to main branch
git pull	Download latest changes
git fetch	Fetch updates without merging

Example

git push

9. Branching
Command	Purpose
git branch	List branches
git branch new-feature	Create branch
git checkout new-feature	Switch branch
git checkout -b new-feature	Create and switch
git switch new-feature	Switch branch (modern command)

Example

git checkout -b python-basics

10. Merge Branches
Command	Purpose
git merge branch-name	Merge a branch
git merge --abort	Cancel merge

Example

git merge python-basics
11. Delete Branches
Command	Purpose
git branch -d branch-name	Delete local branch
git branch -D branch-name	Force delete
git push origin --delete branch-name	Delete remote branch

12. Undo Changes
Command	Purpose
git restore file.txt	Undo file changes
git restore --staged file.txt	Unstage a file
git reset HEAD file.txt	Remove from staging
git reset --hard	Discard all local changes (⚠️ use carefully)

13. View Differences
Command	Purpose
git diff	Show file differences
git diff --staged	Compare staged changes

14. Stash (Temporary Save)
Command	Purpose
git stash	Save unfinished work temporarily
git stash list	Show stashes
git stash pop	Restore latest stash

Useful when you need to switch tasks without committing incomplete work.

15. Tags
Command	Purpose
git tag	List tags
git tag v1.0	Create tag
git push origin v1.0	Push tag

16. Repository Information
Command	Purpose
git remote -v	Show remotes
git branch -a	Show all branches
git show	Show latest commit details

17. Useful History Commands
git log
git log --oneline
git log --graph
git log --all

18. Clone Specific Branch
git clone -b development <repository-url>

19. Rename Branch
git branch -m old-name new-name

20. Remove Untracked Files

Preview first:

git clean -n

Delete:

git clean -f

⚠️ This permanently deletes untracked files.